              "review_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k7UJg2E-TyU&t=0s",
              "start_seconds": 0,
              "end_seconds": 144,
              "label": "Live demo: plotting categorical data with plt.bar()",
              "summary": "The instructor defines two parallel lists — food-group category names and daily-serving counts — then calls plt.bar(), passing the category names directly as the x argument and the counts as heights. The resulting chart appears with the category labels along the x-axis and bar heights reflecting each count, showing that string names work as x-positions without any numeric conversion.",
