    {
      "step_id": "tile_viz_bar_histograms.s07",
      "type": "explainer",
      "concept_ids": [
        "viz.histograms"
      ],
      "eyebrow": "histograms",
      "title": "Seeing the Distribution with a Histogram",
      "lede": "A histogram bins a numeric variable and draws one bar per bin — revealing the shape of the distribution rather than individual values.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_viz_bar_histograms.s07.b02",
          "role": "intro",
          "text": "A bar chart compares categories, but delivery times are a numeric variable. You might instead want to see how those times are distributed — how many deliveries were fast, how many were slow, and whether most cluster in the middle. A histogram answers that question.",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "viz.histograms"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "viz.histograms#tb1"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "viz.histograms#f1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_viz_bar_histograms.s07.b03",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "text": "`plt.hist(x, bins=...)` uses `numpy.histogram` to bin the data in x, count the number of values in each bin, and draw the result as bars. `plt.hist(orders['delivery_time_minutes'])` bins every delivery time and shows how many orders fall into each time range.",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "viz.histograms"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "viz.histograms#tb2"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "viz.histograms#f1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_viz_bar_histograms.s07.b04",
          "role": "syntax",
          "text": "The `bins` parameter defaults to `rcParams['hist.bins']`, which defaults to 10. Passing an integer sets that many equal-width bins; passing a sequence sets explicit bin edges; passing a string such as `'auto'` selects a binning strategy automatically.",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "viz.histograms"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "viz.histograms#tb3"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "viz.histograms#f2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "before_after",
          "block_id": "tile_viz_bar_histograms.s07.b05",
          "before": {
            "type": "code_walkthrough",
            "block_id": "tile_viz_bar_histograms.s07.b01.before",
            "language": "python",
            "code": "# Delivery times as a sorted list — shape is not visible\nprint(sorted(orders['delivery_time_minutes'].tolist()))",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "start_line": 2,
                "end_line": 2,
                "text": "A sorted list shows individual values but not the distribution shape"
              }
            ],
            "reveal": "line_by_line",
            "lineage": {
              "concept_ids": [
                "viz.histograms"
              ],
              "teaching_block_ids": [
                "viz.histograms#tb1"
              ],
              "fact_ids": [
                "viz.histograms#f1"
              ]
            }
          },
          "after": {
            "type": "code_walkthrough",
            "block_id": "tile_viz_bar_histograms.s07.b01.after",
            "language": "python",
            "code": "plt.hist(orders['delivery_time_minutes'], bins=20)",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "start_line": 1,
                "end_line": 1,
                "text": "plt.hist bins the values and draws one bar per bin, revealing the distribution shape"
              }
            ],
            "reveal": "line_by_line",
