          "role": "misconception",
          "text": "Bar charts are easy to interpret because the eye compares lengths from a common baseline. If Kano averages 30 minutes and Lagos 25, bars starting at 20 are 10 and 5 units tall — Kano's bar looks twice as long even though its average is only 5 minutes higher. Keep the baseline at 0 so lengths stay proportional to values.",
